fix(ai): zombie "agent running" state after turn end + attachments dropped while busy

Two stacked bugs behind the same symptom:

1. Zombie busy state. approvalsPending in AgentRunBridge counts
   `approval-requested` parts across ALL history. A stale part (aborted
   run, errored turn, killed approval) pins agentMeta in
   "awaiting-approval" forever: the status pill keeps spinning after the
   agent finished its turn, sends are blocked/redirected to the steering
   queue, and the user's only escape was the Stop button (whose handler
   strips these parts - the manual workaround).

   Fix: releaseStaleApprovalsOnly (chatStore) + a reaper effect in
   AgentRunBridge. Discrimination is critical - a LIVE approval card
   pauses the run with SDK status "ready", so "not running" alone cannot
   mean "stale". A pending part is stale when:
     - it is on an assistant message that is NOT the last assistant
       message (its turn is over), or
     - the chat status is "error" (the card can never resolve).
   The last assistant message with non-error status is spared. Messages
   reduced to zero parts are dropped; visible text is preserved.

2. Attachments dropped on redirect. When isBusy, the composer queued
   only the raw TEXT as the steering message - images, text-file chips,
   selections, and snippets were silently discarded. The user attached an
   image with text, only the text went through; they had to stop the
   agent and resend to get the image across.

   Fix: submit() now composes the full message parts FIRST (same path
   for both cases), then either sends directly (idle) or queues the
   complete parts array as the steering payload. steeringMessage in the
   store changed from string to UIMessagePart[]; AgentRunBridge sends
   the parts as-is. The slash-command "handled" branch also clears
   picked attachments now.

Tests: new chatStore.test.ts - stale/live/error/no-op discrimination
via a mirror implementation + store export contract (parts-typed
steering message). 256 tests pass, tsc clean.
